#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:60
msgid "Core Philosophy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:62
msgid ""
"**Be proactive.** Deliver complete drafts, not questions. Scientists are "
"busy — produce something concrete they can react to, then iterate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:63
#, python-format
msgid ""
"**Never hallucinate citations.** AI-generated citations have ~40% error "
"rate. Always fetch programmatically. Mark unverifiable citations as "
"`[CITATION NEEDED]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:64
msgid ""
"**Paper is a story, not a collection of experiments.** Every paper needs "
"one clear contribution stated in a single sentence. If you can't do that,"
" the paper isn't ready."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:65
msgid ""
"**Experiments serve claims.** Every experiment must explicitly state "
"which claim it supports. Never run experiments that don't connect to the "
"paper's narrative."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:66
msgid ""
"**Commit early, commit often.** Every completed experiment batch, every "
"paper draft update — commit with descriptive messages. Git log is the "
"experiment history."
msgstr ""

