"**Why?** Most reviewers form judgments before reaching your methods. "
"Readers encounter your paper as: title → abstract → introduction → "
"figures → maybe the rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:833
msgid "Writing Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:851
msgid "Two-Pass Refinement Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:853
msgid ""
"When drafting with an AI agent, use a **two-pass** approach (proven "
"effective in SakanaAI's AI-Scientist pipeline):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:855
msgid ""
"**Pass 1 — Write + immediate refine per section:** For each section, "
"write a complete draft, then immediately refine it in the same context. "
"This catches local issues (clarity, flow, completeness) while the section"
" is fresh."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:858
msgid ""
"**Pass 2 — Global refinement with full-paper context:** After all "
"sections are drafted, revisit each section with awareness of the complete"
" paper. This catches cross-section issues: redundancy, inconsistent "
"terminology, narrative flow, and gaps where one section promises "
"something another doesn't deliver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:871
msgid "LaTeX Error Checklist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:873
msgid ""
"Append this checklist to every refinement prompt. These are the most "
"common errors when LLMs write LaTeX:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:890
msgid "Step 5.0: Title"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:892
msgid ""
"The title is the single most-read element of the paper. It determines "
"whether anyone clicks through to the abstract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:894
msgid "**Good titles**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:895
msgid ""
"State the contribution or finding: \"Autoreason: When Iterative LLM "
"Refinement Works and Why It Fails\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:896
msgid ""
"Highlight a surprising result: \"Scaling Data-Constrained Language "
"Models\" (implies you can)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:897
msgid ""
"Name the method + what it does: \"DPO: Direct Preference Optimization of "
"Language Models\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:899
msgid "**Bad titles**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:900
msgid "Too generic: \"An Approach to Improving Language Model Outputs\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:901
msgid "Too long: anything over ~15 words"
