#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1515
msgid "Phase 6: Self-Review & Revision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1517
msgid ""
"**Goal**: Simulate the review process before submission. Catch weaknesses"
" early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1519
msgid "Step 6.1: Simulate Reviews (Ensemble Pattern)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1521
msgid ""
"Generate reviews from multiple perspectives. The key insight from "
"automated research pipelines (notably SakanaAI's AI-Scientist): "
"**ensemble reviewing with a meta-reviewer produces far more calibrated "
"feedback than a single review pass.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1523
msgid "**Step 1: Generate N independent reviews** (N=3-5)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1525
msgid ""
"Use different models or temperature settings. Each reviewer sees only the"
" paper, not other reviews. **Default to negative bias** — LLMs have well-"
"documented positivity bias in evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1554
msgid "**Step 2: Meta-review (Area Chair aggregation)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1556
msgid "Feed all N reviews to a meta-reviewer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1576
msgid "**Step 3: Reflection loop** (optional, 2-3 rounds)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1578
msgid ""
"Each reviewer can refine their review after seeing the meta-review. Use "
"an early termination sentinel: if the reviewer responds \"I am done\" (no"
" changes), stop iterating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1580
msgid ""
"**Model selection for reviewing**: Reviewing is best done with the "
"strongest available model, even if you wrote the paper with a cheaper "
"one. The reviewer model should be chosen independently from the writing "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1582
msgid ""
"**Few-shot calibration**: If available, include 1-2 real published "
"reviews from the target venue as examples. This dramatically improves "
"score calibration. See [references/reviewer-guidelines.md](references"
"/reviewer-guidelines.md) for example reviews."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1584
msgid "Step 6.1b: Visual Review Pass (VLM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1586
msgid ""
"Text-only review misses an entire class of problems: figure quality, "
"layout issues, visual consistency. If you have access to a vision-capable"
" model, run a separate **visual review** on the compiled PDF:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1601
msgid ""
"This catches problems that text-based review cannot: a plot with "
"illegible axis labels, a figure placed 3 pages from its first reference, "
"inconsistent color palettes between Figure 2 and Figure 5, or a table "
"that's clearly wider than the column width."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1603
msgid "Step 6.1c: Claim Verification Pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1605
msgid ""
"After simulated reviews, run a separate verification pass. This catches "
"factual errors that reviewers might miss:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:1615
msgid ""
"For agent-based workflows: delegate verification to a **fresh sub-agent**"
" that receives only the paper text and the raw result files. The fresh "
"context prevents confirmation bias — the verifier doesn't \"remember\" "
"what the results were supposed to be."
msgstr ""

