#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2041
msgid "Paper Types Beyond Empirical ML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2043
msgid ""
"The main pipeline above targets empirical ML papers. Other paper types "
"require different structures and evidence standards. See [references"
"/paper-types.md](references/paper-types.md) for detailed guidance on each"
" type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2045
msgid "Theory Papers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2047
msgid ""
"**Structure**: Introduction → Preliminaries (definitions, notation) → "
"Main Results (theorems) → Proof Sketches → Discussion → Full Proofs "
"(appendix)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2049
msgid "**Key differences from empirical papers:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2050
msgid ""
"Contribution is a theorem, bound, or impossibility result — not "
"experimental numbers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2051
msgid "Methods section replaced by \"Preliminaries\" and \"Main Results\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2052
msgid ""
"Proofs are the evidence, not experiments (though empirical validation of "
"theory is welcome)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2053
msgid "Proof sketches in main text, full proofs in appendix is standard practice"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2054
msgid ""
"Experimental section is optional but strengthens the paper if it "
"validates theoretical predictions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2056
msgid "**Proof writing principles:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2057
msgid "State theorems formally with all assumptions explicit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2058
msgid "Provide intuition before formal proof (\"The key insight is...\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2059
msgid "Proof sketches should convey the main idea in 0.5-1 page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2060
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Use `\\begin{proof}...\\end{proof}` environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2061
msgid ""
"Number assumptions and reference them in theorems: \"Under Assumptions "
"1-3, ...\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2063
msgid "Survey / Tutorial Papers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2065
msgid ""
"**Structure**: Introduction → Taxonomy / Organization → Detailed Coverage"
" → Open Problems → Conclusion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2067
#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2078
#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2089
msgid "**Key differences:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2068
msgid ""
"Contribution is the organization, synthesis, and identification of open "
"problems — not new methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2069
msgid ""
"Must be comprehensive within scope (reviewers will check for missing "
"references)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2070
msgid "Requires a clear taxonomy or organizational framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2071
msgid ""
"Value comes from connections between works that individual papers don't "
"make"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2072
msgid ""
"Best venues: TMLR (survey track), JMLR, Foundations and Trends in ML, ACM"
" Computing Surveys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2074
msgid "Benchmark Papers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2076
msgid ""
"**Structure**: Introduction → Task Definition → Dataset Construction → "
"Baseline Evaluation → Analysis → Intended Use & Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2079
msgid ""
"Contribution is the benchmark itself — it must fill a genuine evaluation "
"gap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2080
msgid ""
"Dataset documentation is mandatory, not optional (see Datasheets, Step "
"5.11)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2081
msgid ""
"Must demonstrate the benchmark is challenging (baselines don't saturate "
"it)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2082
msgid ""
"Must demonstrate the benchmark measures what you claim it measures "
"(construct validity)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2083
msgid ""
"Best venues: NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks track, ACL (resource papers), "
"LREC-COLING"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2085
msgid "Position Papers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2087
msgid ""
"**Structure**: Introduction → Background → Thesis / Argument → Supporting"
" Evidence → Counterarguments → Implications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2090
msgid "Contribution is an argument, not a result"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2091
msgid "Must engage seriously with counterarguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2092
msgid "Evidence can be empirical, theoretical, or logical analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/research-paper-writing_SKILL.md:2093
msgid "Best venues: ICML (position track), workshops, TMLR"
msgstr ""

